  "templateCanonicalPlanTitle": "Canonical Plan",
  "templateCanonicalPlanDescription": "Read the whole Bible in the traditional order, from Genesis to Revelation.",
  "templateCanonicalPlanDetails": "This plan follows the classic order of the biblical books as found in most Christian Bibles.\nYou can change the duration (6 months, 1 year, 2 years…), select only some books, or choose your reading days.\nIdeal as a flexible base to build your own complete journey.",
  "templateChronologicalPlanTitle": "Chronological Plan",
  "templateChronologicalPlanDescription": "Read the Bible in the historical order of events and writing.",
  "templateChronologicalPlanDetails": "This plan places the books and passages in their presumed historical context to better understand how the biblical story unfolds.\nPerfect for following the narrative thread of biblical revelation.\nYou can adjust the duration, and remove or add books depending on your study goal.",
  "templateNewTestamentTitle": "New Testament",
  "templateNewTestamentDescription": "Discover the life of Jesus, the birth of the Church and the apostolic teaching.",
  "templateNewTestamentDetails": "The 27 books of the New Testament in a journey that adapts to your pace.\nYou can read intensively (30 days) or progressively (3 to 6 months).",
  "templateOldTestamentTitle": "Old Testament",
  "templateOldTestamentDescription": "Explore the Law, the history of Israel, the poetic books and the prophets.",
  "templateOldTestamentDetails": "The 39 books of the Old Testament, adjustable to your duration.\nYou can select only certain sections.",
  "templateGospelsTitle": "The Gospels",
  "templateGospelsDescription": "Matthew, Mark, Luke and John in a journey centered on the life of Jesus.",
  "templateGospelsDetails": "Ideal for discovering or rediscovering the person and work of Christ.\nYou can add the book of Acts or adjust the duration (2 weeks to 3 months).\nPerfect for a small group or a new believer.",
  "templatePsalmsTitle": "The Psalms",
  "templatePsalmsDescription": "150 psalms to nourish prayer and meditation.",
  "templatePsalmsDetails": "A spiritual journey centered on worship, repentance and trust in God.\nChoose your pace: 1 psalm a day or several per reading.\nCan be combined with Proverbs for a balance between prayer and wisdom.",
  "templateProverbsTitle": "The Proverbs",
  "templateProverbsDescription": "31 chapters of practical wisdom for everyday life.",
  "templateProverbsDetails": "An ideal plan for a monthly reading (1 chapter a day).\nCan be paired with Ecclesiastes or Song of Solomon to go deeper into wisdom literature.\nSimple, short and immediately applicable.",
  "templateMcheyneTitle": "M'Cheyne Plan",
  "templateMcheyneDescription": "A parallel reading of the Old and New Testaments.",
  "templateMcheyneDetails": "Created by Robert Murray M'Cheyne, this plan offers a parallel reading of the Old and New Testaments.\nThe passages are predefined and follow the original structure.\nYou simply choose the start date.",
  "templateBibleYearLigueTitle": "Bible in 1 Year (Ligue)",
  "templateBibleYearLigueDescription": "A balanced daily reading of the Old Testament, Psalms, Proverbs and New Testament",
  "templateBibleYearLigueDetails": "Each day offers a passage from the Old Testament, a Psalm, a Proverb and a passage from the New Testament.\nA structured, predefined plan, ideal for reading together as a church.",
  "templateRevolutionaryTitle": "Revolutionary Plan",
  "templateRevolutionaryDescription": "25 readings per month with built-in rest days.",
  "templateRevolutionaryDetails": "A structured plan that encourages consistency without overload.\nThe rest days let you catch up or meditate.\nFixed structure: just choose your start date.",
  "templateHornerTitle": "Horner Plan",
  "templateHornerDescription": "Intensive method: 10 chapters a day in parallel readings.",
  "templateHornerDetails": "Designed by Professor Grant Horner, this plan splits the Bible into 10 separate lists read at the same time.\nVery demanding, it encourages immersion and repetition of the texts.\nFully predefined structure.",
